From 43c283e690b509f13fb8ece0484009e400dc4251 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moritz Utcke <moritz.utcke@gmx.de>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:55:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Move a running tool call's task to the background
 (_session/background_tasks)

The SDK's backgroundTasks (Ctrl+B in the terminal) had no ACP way in. _session/background_tasks {sessionId, toolCallId?} moves the foreground task of a tool call (a Bash command, a subagent), or all of them, to the background without cancelling the turn: the tool call returns at once and the task runs on. Advertised as _meta.backgroundTasks on v1; not on v2, which doesn't serve it.
